I've never tried the windows version.  On my linux version from the
dat directory I have to do:

../util/makedefs -e
../util/dgn_comp dungeon.pdf

you don't actually run dgn_comp against the .def file, but against a
".pdf" that makedefs creates.  BTW that .pdf is nothing like what most
people think of pdfs.

Potentially useful links:
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Dungeon.def
http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Makedefs
http://members.shaw.ca/rob.ellwood/sources.txt

As far as I can tell, there isn't a current updated guide for adding
levels, branches, or other things to nethack.  If there is I'd love to
see it.  From the above links I've managed to figure out how to add my
own levels and branches and even a new monster.  Haven't been able to
add an artifact yet or even a new type of weapon (and certainly
haven't been able to add a new type of invocation ceremony without
causing a segmentation fault).  I get the feeling other than the dev
team, very few people actually try to add anything to the game or if
they do they don't tell the secrets to doing so.

